IMPORT prelude

-- Multi-Level Marketing and Pyramid Selling (Prohibition) Act 1973 (Singapore) -- what a pyramid selling scheme is and what counts
-- as a "benefit" (s 2), the offence of promoting, participating or holding out (s 3), registering a business name or incorporating
-- a company for such a scheme (ss 4, 5), liability of directors and managers (s 6), and the extra penalty that strips the benefit
-- received (s 7).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MLMPSPA1973.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment in its
-- Legislative History is Act 29 of 2014 (Business Names Registration Act 2014, commenced 3 January 2016). The deposit's arrangement
-- of sections is out of step with the body; this encoding follows the body's numbering (ss 1 to 10).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone invited to "join" a sales network, recruit friends or sign up under
-- an upline meets it, and it makes the participant, not only the organiser, an offender. SCOPED to the whole operative Act except
-- what follows. Not encoded: s 2(3) (winding up of foreign companies), s 7(3) (offences taken into consideration), s 7(4) (damages
-- unaffected) beyond a comment, s 8 (District Court may impose the full penalty), s 9 (Act prevails over the Business Names
-- Registration Act 2014 and Companies Act 1967) and s 10 (regulations). Any order made by the Minister under s 2(2) excluding
-- schemes was NOT retrieved; it is modelled only as a flag.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Multi-Level Marketing and Pyramid Selling (Prohibition) Act 1973`

§§ `2(1), (2) -- pyramid selling scheme or arrangement`

-- s 2(1): "multi-level marketing scheme or arrangement" has THE SAME MEANING as "pyramid selling scheme or arrangement".
-- "pyramid selling scheme or arrangement" means any scheme for the distribution or purported distribution of a commodity by which
-- (a) a person may in any manner acquire a commodity, or a right or licence to acquire it, "for sale, lease, licence or other
-- distribution"; (b) that person receives any benefit, directly or indirectly, as a result of (i) "the recruitment, acquisition,
-- action or performance of one or more additional participants" or (ii) the sale, lease, licence or other distribution of the
-- commodity by one or more additional participants; and (c) any benefit "is or may be received by any other person who promotes, or
-- participates in, the scheme" (other than the person in (a) or an additional participant in (b)).
-- "commodity" means any goods, service, right or other property, tangible or intangible, capable of sale, lease or licence.
-- s 2(2): does not include schemes or classes of scheme "that the Minister may by order prescribe", on the order's terms.
DECLARE Scheme HAS
    `a person may acquire a commodity or a right to it for distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person benefits from recruiting or the performance of additional participants` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person benefits from distribution by additional participants` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some other promoter or participant may benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded by order of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the scheme` IS A Scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the scheme is a pyramid selling scheme` IF
        `the scheme`'s `a person may acquire a commodity or a right to it for distribution`
    AND (    `the scheme`'s `that person benefits from recruiting or the performance of additional participants`
         OR  `the scheme`'s `that person benefits from distribution by additional participants`)
    AND `the scheme`'s `some other promoter or participant may benefit`
    AND (NOT `the scheme`'s `excluded by order of the Minister`)

§§ `2(1) -- benefit`

-- "benefit" includes "any gratuity, commission, cross commission, bonus, refund, discount, dividend and any other payment, service or
-- advantage of whatever description", but does not include (a) "the purchase of a sample of a commodity furnished at a price not
-- exceeding the cost of the sample and which is not for resale"; and (b) "time and effort spent in pursuit of sales, distribution or
-- recruiting activities".
DECLARE Advantage IS ONE OF
    `a commission`
    `a cross commission`
    `a bonus`
    `a refund`
    `a discount`
    `a dividend`
    `a free service`
    `a sample bought at or below cost and not for resale`
    `time and effort spent recruiting`

GIVEN `the advantage` IS AN Advantage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advantage is a benefit` IF
    CONSIDER `the advantage`
    WHEN `a sample bought at or below cost and not for resale` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `time and effort spent recruiting` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `sample price` IS A NUMBER, `cost of the sample` IS A NUMBER, `bought for resale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sample purchase is excluded from benefit` IF
    `sample price` AT MOST `cost of the sample` AND (NOT `bought for resale`)

§§ `3 -- promoting, participating or holding out`

-- s 3(1): "It is unlawful for any person to promote or participate in a multi-level marketing scheme or arrangement or a pyramid
-- selling scheme or arrangement or to hold out that the person is promoting or participating in such a scheme or arrangement."
-- (2): fine not exceeding $200,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 5 years or both.
-- s 2(1): "promote" includes "to manage, form, operate, carry on, engage in or otherwise to organise".
--
-- INFERENCE: holding out is encoded as an offence whether or not the scheme held out really is a pyramid selling scheme; the text
-- makes the claim itself unlawful, and does not say the scheme must exist.
GIVEN `the scheme` IS A Scheme, `promotes it` IS A BOOLEAN, `participates in it` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds out as promoting or participating` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes section 3` IF
        (`the scheme is a pyramid selling scheme` `the scheme` AND (`promotes it` OR `participates in it`))
    OR  `holds out as promoting or participating`

§§ `3(2), 4(2), 5(2) -- maximum punishments`

-- s 4(1): a person "must not apply to be registered under the Business Names Registration Act 2014 under any business name in respect
-- of any business that is designed to promote" such a scheme. s 5(1): no company proposing to promote such a scheme "is to be
-- incorporated or registered under the Companies Act 1967". All three offences: "a fine not exceeding $200,000 or to imprisonment for
-- a term not exceeding 5 years or to both".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `promoting or participating, s 3`
    `holding out, s 3`
    `applying for a business name, s 4`
    `a company obtaining incorporation, s 5`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS 200000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS 5

GIVEN `designed to promote a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied for business name registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant contravenes section 4` IF
    `designed to promote a scheme` AND `applied for business name registration`

-- s 5(2): where a company designed to promote such a scheme obtains incorporation or registration, "that company and every officer
-- of that company shall be guilty of an offence". s 5 itself states no defence for the officer; the s 6(2) defence is written for
-- "the individual mentioned in subsection (1)" of s 6 (that reading is an inference).
GIVEN `designed to promote a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN, `obtained incorporation or registration` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the company or one of its officers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guilty under section 5` IF
    `designed to promote a scheme` AND `obtained incorporation or registration` AND `is the company or one of its officers`

§§ `6 -- offences by bodies corporate`

-- s 6(1): if the offender is a company, "every individual who at the time the offence was committed was a director, general manager,
-- manager, secretary or other officer of the company concerned in the management of the company or who was purporting to act in any
-- such capacity" is deemed guilty with it. (2): a defence if the individual PROVES the offence was committed "without his or her
-- consent or connivance" AND that he or she exercised the diligence he or she ought to have. (3): "company" includes any body
-- corporate and "a firm or other association of individuals".
--
-- Read here as: the named offices are caught outright; "concerned in the management" qualifies only "other officer". That reading
-- is an inference; the sentence can also be read as qualifying every office.
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `director`
    `general manager`
    `manager`
    `secretary`
    `other officer concerned in management`
    `officer not concerned in management`
    `ordinary employee`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is caught by section 6` IF
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `officer not concerned in management` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `ordinary employee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the company committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the office` IS AN Office, `purported to act in such an office` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is guilty under section 6` IF
        `the company committed an offence`
    AND (`the office is caught by section 6` `the office` OR `purported to act in such an office`)
    AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved due diligence`))

§§ `7 -- penalty stripping the benefit`

-- s 7(1): where a court convicts a person "of committing an offence of promoting or participating in" such a scheme under s 3(2),
-- then if (a) the person received any benefit as a result and (b) it is a sum of money or its value can be assessed, the court "is,
-- in addition to imposing on that person any other punishment, to order that person to pay as a penalty ... a sum not exceeding the
-- amount of or, in the opinion of the court, the value of the benefit received", recoverable as a fine.
-- (2): for a PARTICIPANT the court "may take into account" any benefit given for the right to participate, or any loss incurred.
-- (4): nothing in (1) affects any right to recover damages from the person.
--
-- The text ties s 7 to promoting or participating; a conviction for holding out, or under s 4 or s 5, does not trigger it.
-- s 7(2) is a discretion, so no netting of the joining fee is computed here; only the ceiling is.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `received a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN, `the benefit is money or can be valued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must order a section 7 penalty` IF
        `received a benefit`
    AND `the benefit is money or can be valued`
    AND CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `promoting or participating, s 3` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `received a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN, `the benefit is money or can be valued` IS A BOOLEAN, `value of the benefit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ceiling of the section 7 penalty` MEANS
    IF `the court must order a section 7 penalty` `the offence` `received a benefit` `the benefit is money or can be valued`
    THEN `value of the benefit`
    ELSE 0
